# Lambda Layer direct dependency list (HUMAN-EDITED SOURCE, Issue #35).
#
# This file is the single human-edited source of the DependenciesLayer
# dependencies. The sibling requirements.txt is GENERATED from this file
# (fully pinned, including all transitive dependencies) and is what SAM's
# PythonPipBuilder actually installs. Do NOT edit requirements.txt directly;
# edit this file and regenerate with the standard compile command
# (see infra/README.md "Layer dependency lock").
#
# boto3/botocore ship with the Lambda managed runtime, so they are excluded
# here (reduces package size, per AWS's recommended practice).
# typer/python-dotenv are CLI-only dependencies not referenced from
# lambda_handlers/services/domain, so they are excluded here too.
#
# Operational hardening item 8: version ranges are capped to the verified range
# (matches pyproject.toml's ranges; keep both files in sync, since the compiled
# requirements.txt is what actually determines what ships in the deployed
# Lambda artifact).
#
# Kept ASCII-only intentionally: some pip build steps (SAM CLI's
# PythonPipBuilder on Windows, requirements-file parsers used by CI tooling)
# default to a non-UTF-8 codec and fail on non-ASCII bytes in this file.
pydantic>=2.13,<3.0
pyyaml>=6.0,<7.0
python-dateutil>=2.9,<3.0
jpholiday>=1.0,<2.0
# yfinance is an unofficial library and the most prone to breaking changes,
# so its range is kept the narrowest.
yfinance>=1.5.2,<1.6.0
# Full-scale candidate universe support (2026-08): used to parse the JPX
# listed-issues file (.xls). Also added to pyproject.toml's realdata extra
# with the same version (this file and pyproject.toml are managed
# independently; the compiled requirements.txt is what actually determines
# the deployed Lambda dependencies, so adding it to only one of the two would
# silently drop it in production).
xlrd>=2.0,<3.0
# Weekly improvement review revamp (2026-08): GitHub App JWT auth for the
# GitHub Issue integration (infrastructure/github/client.py, used by
# WeeklyReviewFunction only). The [crypto] extra pulls in the cryptography
# package needed for RS256 signing (not otherwise present in this layer).
PyJWT[crypto]>=2.10,<3.0
# Explicit for two reasons (Issue #35): (1) pandas/pydantic declare tzdata
# only under sys_platform == "win32" markers, so the pre-lock production
# layers (built by pip on a Windows host) always contained it, and the
# initial lock must match that verified set exactly; (2) it guarantees the
# IANA timezone database for zoneinfo on the Lambda runtime regardless of
# what the OS image ships. Do not remove without a dedicated issue.
tzdata>=2026.3,<2027.0
